 Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33ebe7dc-2640-5c30-a725-5b80729c055c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446023} {:answer/id #uuid "5ae07b21-e2d7-5206-b65f-7c1571c68e32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446024} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd72eca-5391-5727-94ab-463621c4a2bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446030} {:answer/id #uuid "df456283-35cc-5343-9064-99b253c7571c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446036} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b58bd4-6483-5919-a713-a3b33ddea143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ae07b21-e2d7-5206-b65f-7c1571c68e32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446024} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d841b72-edb4-5a8f-91af-b6d5a776d196" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ed79229-2ecc-57da-b369-71aea5f1638c" :question/math-academy-id "q-79344" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$\n\nII. If $C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$\n\nIII. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $B$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124509 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11bd5b8c-479c-5cc6-b6bf-6871d03b08d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436673} {:answer/id #uuid "5cb2151a-b33e-521e-b8b0-24402371cbfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436675} {:answer/id #uuid "7de2f3de-7c9b-5a4b-bf43-493cdbc1ac7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436676} {:answer/id #uuid "b84ac634-ebd3-56af-8b44-0c0dd0d7b70e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436677} {:answer/id #uuid "c9a9fef4-70fb-5285-b43b-261546c9e8bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11bd5b8c-479c-5cc6-b6bf-6871d03b08d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436673} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4adc5e4-eeb4-5d02-8d02-ca9f53944067" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436682}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e39062c0-8f9b-52cc-adaa-1df745d5f896" :question/math-academy-id "q-79346" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and the $4$th columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1+1+2=4.\n$$"}]}
